1
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:19,937
HELLO, TWENTY - WONHEE

2
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:22,773
ULTIMATE VIBE CENTRAL
MANGWON-DONG

3
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:26,276
LIVELY STREETS WITH ENERGETIC YOUNG PEOPLE

4
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,028
Hello, everyone.

5
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,781
This is the seventh episode
of Hello, Twenty - Wonhee.

6
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:34,952
I'm looking forward to the new experience
I'll have with today's guest.

7
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:36,954
We're in Mangwon-dong today.

8
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,413
What's going on?

9
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:39,790
Have you ever been here?

10
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:43,001
I think just once outside of work.

11
00:00:43,085 --> 00:00:45,337
Here in Mangwon-dong,

12
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:48,423
you're about to embark on a journey
of self-discovery.

13
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,967
Self-discovery? Well, here I am.

14
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:50,968
Sorry.

15
00:00:51,051 --> 00:00:52,010
QUICK APOLOGY

16
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:54,763
WE START TO FIND OURSELVES AT 20

17
00:00:55,264 --> 00:00:59,184
FIRST STEP IN SELF-DISCOVERY:
DEVELOP YOUR OWN TASTE

18
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,271
SEVENTH ITEM ON WONHEE'S BUCKET LIST

19
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:05,190
FIGURE OUT MY TASTE

20
00:01:05,274 --> 00:01:07,568
We prepared a questionnaire for you.

21
00:01:07,651 --> 00:01:10,070
- A questionnaire?
- Here you go.

22
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:11,989
- I see.
- Your goal today is

23
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:15,826
figuring out who you are as a person.

24
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:19,121
An all-rounder guide is waiting for you.

25
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:21,790
Is she who I'm thinking of?

26
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:24,501
<i>The multi-faceted entertainer.</i>

27
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,878
- Shall we go meet her?
- Sure.

28
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:28,672
I've been dying to meet her.

29
00:01:29,006 --> 00:01:34,094
My group members and I
are all huge fans of hers.

30
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:38,265
I can't wait to learn
how to crack jokes from her.

31
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:44,187
I hope to learn as much as I can
from our amazing girlie today.

32
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:46,648
I'll see you soon, girlie.

33
00:01:46,857 --> 00:01:49,818
MEETUP SPOT:
A VINTAGE SHOP IN MANGWON-DONG

34
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:51,695
3 SECONDS AWAY

35
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:53,655
I've wanted to visit this place.

36
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,074
"An invitation to happiness."

37
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:58,577
- Hello.
- Gosh, hello.

38
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,621
- Hello.
- Gosh, hello.

39
00:02:00,704 --> 00:02:01,913
EPISODE 7 GIRLIE
YOUTUBER CHARLES

40
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:03,040
Am I watching YouTube?

41
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:05,083
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

42
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:06,293
SHY AT FIRST MEETING

43
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,878
Can I call you by your first name?

44
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,421
Of course, Ms. Wonhee.

45
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:10,714
Speak casually, Charles.

46
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,257
- May I?
- Sure.

47
00:02:12,341 --> 00:02:13,925
CASUAL TONE, FORMAL GESTURE
Thanks.

48
00:02:14,009 --> 00:02:15,427
You can talk casually, too.

49
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:17,512
Let's both speak casually.

50
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,014
Okay, I'd love that.

51
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,266
COMPLETELY DISARMED

52
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:22,726
Let's both talk casually.

53
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:24,061
- Shall we?
- Sure.

54
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:24,978
All right.

55
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,355
- Starting now, okay?
- Okay.

56
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:29,650
Whoever talks formally
performs a party trick as a penalty.

57
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:30,817
I don't have any.

58
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:32,027
Then make one up, Ms. Charles.

59
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,989
OH, NO

60
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:37,658
A PENALTY IN JUST 5 SECONDS

61
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:39,159
Show me your party trick.

62
00:02:39,618 --> 00:02:40,577
NOSTRIL FLARING

63
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,412
I can do something similar.

64
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:43,580
NOSTRIL COLLAPSING

65
00:02:43,622 --> 00:02:44,748
NOSTRIL PARTY TRICK

66
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,583
I can do it, too.

67
00:02:46,667 --> 00:02:48,085
SQUEEZES NOSTRILS SHUT

68
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,294
Wait, but...

69
00:02:49,378 --> 00:02:50,420
NOSTRIL TRICKS GALORE

70
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:53,382
Can you move your nose like this?

71
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,425
Your nose, not your upper lip.

72
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:57,886
Your nose, not your nostrils.

73
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:00,889
- I can't do that.
- Great, mine's unique.

74
00:03:01,765 --> 00:03:02,891
What brings you here?

75
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,811
I'm here to shoot an episode with you.

76
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:07,145
Well, it's a date.

77
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:08,563
Why did you ask me here?

78
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:11,733
It's the perfect place
to figure out what you like.

79
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:14,653
That's a good choice.
I don't really know my own taste.

80
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,947
- Did you just read off the script?
- No.

81
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,449
IT'S A QUESTIONNAIRE
I don't have a set taste yet.

82
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:20,534
- Really?
- Yeah.

83
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,577
- Don't you like digicams?
- Yes, I do.

84
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,495
On your Instagram--

85
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:26,998
The moment I walked in,
these digicams caught my eye.

86
00:03:27,082 --> 00:03:29,000
- I've had my eyes on it, too.
- Really?

87
00:03:29,084 --> 00:03:30,752
- Let's settle it with a game.
- Right.

88
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:32,504
- Are you paying for everything?
- Sure.

89
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:33,964
Then you're the boss.

90
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,465
Want to call me "boss"?

91
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:37,300
Yes, boss.

92
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:38,844
By the way,

93
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:41,263
- you're so pretty.
- What on earth?

94
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:44,975
Seriously, you're so cute.

95
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:47,519
THAT'S TOO MUCH
My gosh. Sorry about that.

96
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,521
I rarely see someone as pretty as you.

97
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,231
Don't you ever check the mirror?

98
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,818
ON ANOTHER LEVEL

99
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,903
- You're something else.
- I'm an idol.

100
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,197
NATURAL AT HYPING PEOPLE UP

101
00:03:59,281 --> 00:04:00,240
What's on that board?

102
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:01,783
My assignment for the day.

103
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:04,995
<i>It's a questionnaire</i>
<i>to help me find what I like.</i>

104
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:08,665
<i>- So many questions, right?</i>
<i>- We can go through them together.</i>

105
00:04:08,707 --> 00:04:10,500
Let's figure out your taste.

106
00:04:10,542 --> 00:04:11,501
LIGHT AND CHEERFUL

107
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:12,878
LOUD AND BOISTEROUS

108
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:13,962
SAME WORDS, DIFFERENT VIBES

109
00:04:14,004 --> 00:04:15,672
Oh, no. We're doomed.

110
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,841
- Sorry, we're good.
- Take it back.

111
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:19,634
I will. Let's have a look around.

112
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,428
Oh, this one is a film camera.

113
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,430
- They are mock-ups.
- Digicams are easier to use.

114
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,556
These are the real things.

115
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:25,974
- That's a film camera.
- Really?

116
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,267
- Is this the only digicam?
- Yes.

117
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,352
OOPS

118
00:04:30,854 --> 00:04:31,855
Let's have a look around.

119
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:33,565
BATTLE DELAYED
Glasses are great, too.

120
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,317
- Shall we try some on?
- The glasses?

121
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:36,735
Totally my dad's vibe.

122
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:37,861
RETRO VIBES

123
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,071
I think these are prescription glasses.

124
00:04:40,155 --> 00:04:41,865
This pair, too. What in the world?

125
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:44,701
MAXIMUM HIPSTER ENERGY

126
00:04:44,743 --> 00:04:45,869
Is it okay to sell these?

127
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:47,204
Don't you feel dizzy?

128
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,914
- Just yesterday...
- Try this on.

129
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,375
BACK IN HIGH SCHOOL

130
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,543
I can't see properly.

131
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:54,878
Have you considered LASIK?

132
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:59,382
I won't be able to wear contacts then,
but they're a must for performers.

133
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:01,635
I can't risk looking too plain on stage.

134
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,304
WHO COULD'VE GUESSED?

135
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:07,432
I'm already worried because my features
are too soft for an idol.

136
00:05:07,516 --> 00:05:08,642
That's nonsense.

137
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,060
- It's the truth.
- Really?

138
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,062
Jeez, haven't you seen other idols?

139
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:14,231
UNFILTERED HONESTY

140
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:17,067
- You're so funny.
- My features aren't strong.

141
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,985
She's got an amazing personality.

142
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:20,695
HEHE

143
00:05:20,737 --> 00:05:22,072
- That looks nice.
- Really?

144
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,616
- Yes, I dig the geek-chic vibe.
- Geek chic?

145
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:25,909
- Get that pair.
- Should I?

146
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:29,037
Don't I remind you of someone
in this outfit?

147
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,455
You know, Mr. Long Legs.

148
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,208
AIR GUITAR

149
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,876
GOING ABOVE AND BEYOND

150
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,962
I'm sorry. I'll try to pull my weight.

151
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,089
WONHEE'S WORK ETHIC
IS GIVING US A WAKEUP CALL

152
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:42,175
I'm an ISFP who tries hard to be outgoing.

153
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:44,928
My best friend is an ISFP, too.

154
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:45,846
- Really?
- Yeah.

155
00:05:45,929 --> 00:05:48,181
The goofball you met earlier
is the real me.

156
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:50,100
WONHEE'S FIRST IMPRESSION

157
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,227
Can you move your nose like this?

158
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:54,771
ISFP'S MIND IS AN ENIGMA

159
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:58,233
I was nervous about meeting you
because I wanted to make you laugh.

160
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:00,902
- Really?
- I wanted to make sure you had fun.

161
00:06:00,944 --> 00:06:03,029
- I'm having fun.
- Really? I'm so glad.

162
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,739
- Let's check out the clothes.
- Okay.

163
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,784
Do you have a signature style now?

164
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,202
Not really.

165
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:12,289
- What kind of style do you like?
- I'm into unique vintage pieces.

166
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:14,833
But I don't want old-fashioned stuff.

167
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:15,917
Let's see.

168
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:18,545
For example, I'd like this better
without the floral pattern.

169
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,005
- This?
- This much is good.

170
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:22,340
I like sparkly vintage pieces
with a unique charm like...

171
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:23,884
Wait, this is so pretty.

172
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:27,804
- Do you think this jacket is for sale?
- I think so.

173
00:06:27,846 --> 00:06:29,055
- I like it.
- Want to take it off?

174
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,891
MANNEQUIN'S ARMS ARE BARE
Too revealing.

175
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:32,017
Like this...

176
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,479
- Wear that to the airport.
- To the airport?

177
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:37,939
- It'd be perfect.
- You think so?

178
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:40,567
Wow, it's really nice.

179
00:06:40,901 --> 00:06:41,985
CHECKS THE MIRROR

180
00:06:42,611 --> 00:06:43,737
How do I look?

181
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,238
- Simply stunning.
- Really?

182
00:06:45,322 --> 00:06:46,740
STARES
Does it suit me?

183
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,158
This is sick.

184
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:50,243
UNFILTERED THOUGHTS

185
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,370
You're so pretty.

186
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:54,414
- Thanks.
- What's it like being you?

187
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:56,833
When I look at my reflection after makeup,

188
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,752
I feel guilty because I look so different.

189
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,295
COMPLIMENT REJECTED

190
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,671
I've talked about this before.

191
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:03,256
What's your favorite style?

192
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,634
I'm actually into quirky pieces.

193
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,844
How's this? It caught my eye right away.

194
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:10,347
I like it. What do you think?

195
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:12,557
- Not my thing.
- Okay.

196
00:07:12,641 --> 00:07:15,727
Let's say I wore something in my video,
and people saw it elsewhere.

197
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:18,521
I want people to say,
"Hey, Charles wore that!"

198
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:19,814
It's all about being memorable.

199
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,858
I even wear an orange puffer jacket
to stand out.

200
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:24,736
I like clothes that really stand out.

201
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:28,198
- I've already picked one out.
- Show me. Which one is it?

202
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,824
Over there. This one.

203
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:32,744
INTENSE VACATION VIBES

204
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:34,037
Isn't it cute?

205
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,372
NOT SURE WHAT TO SAY

206
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,581
It is cute, but...

207
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:39,793
It's even cinched at the waist. So extra.

208
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:41,878
- I--
- But isn't that cuter?

209
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:43,213
<i>Seriously?</i>

210
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:44,255
SHOCKING TASTES ALL AROUND

211
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:46,424
CHECKS THE MIRROR

212
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:48,051
I want to wear this in summer.

213
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:50,428
"Charles wore this, didn't she?"

214
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:51,888
Isn't it so cute?

215
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:54,724
- I swear I'll be back.
- I'm buying this. It's so cute.

216
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:58,061
- Isn't it so cute?
- It is!

217
00:07:58,144 --> 00:07:59,980
If only I were smaller...

218
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:01,439
- Won't it fit you?
- No way.

219
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,984
- I'm sure it will.
- I guarantee you it won't.

220
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,235
But it will fit.

221
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,362
I can prove you wrong.

222
00:08:07,404 --> 00:08:08,446
Maybe not, I guess.

223
00:08:08,989 --> 00:08:10,407
It's so cute, though.

224
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,450
- It's totally my style.
- Really?

225
00:08:12,534 --> 00:08:16,454
I used to be a huge floral fan,
but I've moved on from that phase.

226
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:18,415
- You're done with it?
- I'm in my sporty era.

227
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:19,332
You are?

228
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:21,626
Isn't this too neon?

229
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,086
No, it's pretty.

230
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:26,089
- It's kind of wrinkly, but it's cute.
- Fair point.

231
00:08:26,131 --> 00:08:28,258
The mesh looks like polka dots.

232
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,301
- Get it. It's so cute.
- I love polka dots.

233
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:31,886
I've never seen one like this.

234
00:08:32,554 --> 00:08:34,389
You're tempting me to buy it.

235
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:35,432
It's just...

236
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,767
"I've never seen one like this."
That did it for me.

237
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:39,436
That's the charm of vintage items.

238
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,770
- Everything is special.
- Right.

239
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,273
- What's your shoe size?
- I'm a size 240.

240
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:44,899
- That's a surprise.
- Really?

241
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:47,110
- What about you?
- You look like a size 220.

242
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,486
You know what?

243
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:49,738
What a pleasant randomness.

244
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:50,905
Randomness?

245
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,407
What's that supposed to mean?

246
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:55,201
I've never heard of that phrase before.

247
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:57,620
Don't people usually say
"an unexpected twist"?

248
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:01,249
It was a nice surprise.

249
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:02,959
- You found it surprisingly charming?
- Yes.

250
00:09:03,001 --> 00:09:04,627
I'll try to read between the lines.

251
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,130
CHECKING OUT ANOTHER SECTION

252
00:09:08,131 --> 00:09:09,257
SWISH, SWISH

253
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:11,801
SWISH, SWISH

254
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,470
- Not our style, right?
- No.

255
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:15,472
- Let's move on.
- That's why you went quiet.

256
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:18,433
Look, that definitely meets your criteria.

257
00:09:18,475 --> 00:09:19,350
What do you think?

258
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:22,312
- It's memorable.
- This dress right here

259
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,564
is giving Paris Fashion Week.

260
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:27,317
Wait, I've been there twice.
I think I saw this on the runway.

261
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:29,527
A SHOCKING EYE-OPENER FOR THE DESIGNERS

262
00:09:30,028 --> 00:09:31,154
What do you think?

263
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:34,824
VERY PARISIAN BAKERY OWNER ENERGY

264
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:35,992
This would suit you.

265
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:38,620
So unique. Don't they have the same vibe?

266
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,622
ALPINE MEADOWS VIBES

267
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:41,664
I'm not sure about this.

268
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:43,333
Why not? It's cute.

269
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:44,334
Super memorable.

270
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,544
Why do you like this shirt
but not these dresses?

271
00:09:46,628 --> 00:09:47,504
About that.

272
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,840
If I pair this top with simple bottoms...

273
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,843
- Whatever, I dig this.
- I get it now.

274
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:56,846
So one piece should be simple

275
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,682
- so the other can pop.
- I have a thing for patchwork, too.

276
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:02,352
- I like these little details.
- I see.

277
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:03,353
NEW KNOWLEDGE GAINED

278
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:04,938
So you like patchwork.

279
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:08,108
- This is cute.
- You really dig this style, huh?

280
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:09,567
Now, put this back.

281
00:10:09,651 --> 00:10:11,027
- You have that one.
- Okay.

282
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:12,946
- Leave it.
- That's cuter, though.

283
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:13,947
IS WONHEE IN SAFE HANDS?

284
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,698
What about this? It's pretty cute.

285
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:16,866
- This--
- Hard pass.

286
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,201
But the patchwork...

287
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,369
I have my standards.

288
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,870
This is a genuine patchwork.

289
00:10:21,204 --> 00:10:22,413
- This is...
- It's a fake?

290
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:23,581
QUICK TO GIVE UP

291
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:26,376
What about this?

292
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,129
- So?
- Is this a scarecrow?

293
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:30,839
I'd chase all the birds away.

294
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,007
It'd be nice not to worry about pigeons.

295
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:34,676
A HUMAN BIRD CONTROL?

296
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:37,804
VINTAGE FASHION MASTER ON RICE PADDY

297
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,223
This section is giving
<i>I'm Sorry, I Love You.</i>

298
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:41,683
What's that?

299
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:42,892
Do you really not know?

300
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,562
AIRED BEFORE SHE WAS BORN
I'm not good with memes.

301
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:48,064
- "Dinner with me or death?"
- I've heard of that.

302
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:49,440
- "Dinner with me or death?"
- Yeah.

303
00:10:49,524 --> 00:10:51,568
Lim Soo-jung wore
something like this on that show.

304
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,444
FINDS A NEW DRESS
This right here...

305
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:55,572
This one has that vibe.

306
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:57,740
<i>My Lovely Sam-soon</i>, right?

307
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:58,700
Sang-soon?

308
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:00,076
<i>My Lovely Sam-soon.</i>

309
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,703
- Haven't watched it, either.
- Really?

310
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,913
Jung Ryeo-won starts crying
in a similar outfit.

311
00:11:03,955 --> 00:11:06,416
- She empties her bag and flops down.
- Out of the blue?

312
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,209
- Like this.
- Randomly?

313
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:09,919
- Holding the top?
- No, wearing it.

314
00:11:09,961 --> 00:11:11,421
- Wearing it?
- In this kind of outfit.

315
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:13,548
It's giving Y2K.

316
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,675
So this is a true vintage clothing store.

317
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,261
Shall we decide on the digicam?

318
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,846
- There's just one.
- Exactly.

319
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,557
Can we take a picture with it?
Does it work?

320
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:25,268
CAMERA ON

321
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:26,895
Wait, can I take your pic?

322
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,106
A SHOT OF WONHEE

323
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,482
- Just one thing.
- Yes?

324
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,818
You were covering the flash.

325
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:36,946
I wondered why the photo came out orange.

326
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:38,448
So cute.

327
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,452
Cute, right?

328
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:43,620
Hey, it's nice.

329
00:11:43,703 --> 00:11:45,121
- Rock-paper-scissors, then?
- Shall we?

330
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:46,456
- You can have it.
- Oh, shoot.

331
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:47,832
- Don't be like that.
- Okay.

332
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:50,293
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

333
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:51,586
- Rock--
- Wait!

334
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:54,088
Best of three or one-off?

335
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,298
- One-off.
- Okay.

336
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,133
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

337
00:11:58,718 --> 00:12:00,762
WINNER, LOSER

338
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,472
- Is it really mine?
- Of course.

339
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,473
For real?

340
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:05,266
I'm a cool 20-year-old girlie.

341
00:12:05,308 --> 00:12:07,727
- Thanks, Wonhee.
- No problem.

342
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,687
NO HESITATION IN USING THE COMPANY CARD
Lucky me.

343
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:11,231
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

344
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:14,484
Let's take many photos with this
to remember our day together.

345
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,486
<i>Let's go to our next stop!</i>

346
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:17,570
<i>Let's go!</i>

347
00:12:17,654 --> 00:12:19,113
<i>Your energy level spiked up.</i>

348
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:20,615
POWER OF SHOPPING

349
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,659
- They know what they're doing here.
- Right?

350
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,702
They set up a photo zone.

351
00:12:24,786 --> 00:12:26,996
A MUST FOR GEN Z: MIRROR SELFIE

352
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:29,666
ON TO THE NEXT DESTINATION

353
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:32,752
- It feels like I'm on <i>Guerrilla Date</i>.
- Right?

354
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,921
- Can we walk arm in arm?
- Of course.

355
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,256
HOLDING CLOSE

356
00:12:36,339 --> 00:12:38,007
Don't people question it

357
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:41,552
- when you tell them your MBTI type?
- Like what?

358
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:43,680
They say things like,
"You can't be an ISFP."

359
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:45,431
- I'm an ENFP.
- You are?

360
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:46,391
I see.

361
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:48,059
Didn't you say you were an ISFP?

362
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:50,687
- No, I said my best friend was.
- Your best friend?

363
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,272
- I misheard that.
- I see.

364
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:54,274
My best friend is an ISFP.

365
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:55,900
CORRECTION

366
00:12:55,984 --> 00:12:58,152
How did you get

367
00:12:58,194 --> 00:12:59,988
- such an awesome personality?
- Me?

368
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,364
You're so chill.

369
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:02,865
Did I ever look like a horrible person?

370
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:05,285
Of course not.

371
00:13:05,368 --> 00:13:06,577
- You're just 20--
- Did I?

372
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,329
No, I'm amazed. That's all.

373
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:11,916
You're so fun to be around,
so I want to match that energy.

374
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,086
To be honest,
you've thrown me off my game.

375
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:17,630
I'm struggling to keep up.

376
00:13:17,714 --> 00:13:21,342
- This is a first for me.
- Right? This isn't your A game.

377
00:13:21,384 --> 00:13:23,011
- It's just--
- Make me laugh.

378
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,220
TEASING HER

379
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:26,389
I'm dying to do that.

380
00:13:26,431 --> 00:13:28,891
- You got me out of my rhythm.
- Tell me a joke.

381
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:30,977
Usually, I'm the clown of the party.

382
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:34,063
But you're making all the jokes,
so I'm at a loss.

383
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:36,065
I don't even know
what I'm supposed to be doing.

384
00:13:36,149 --> 00:13:37,191
- You feel me?
- Yeah.

385
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:39,444
- I'm losing my mind.
- I'm going to run out of steam soon.

386
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,571
- You can pick things up then.
- Okay.

387
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:42,947
Another vintage clothing store.

388
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:46,075
Mangwon-dong is the perfect place
to discover your taste.

389
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:48,786
I'm coming back tomorrow.
I actually have a date.

390
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:50,079
With who?

391
00:13:50,121 --> 00:13:51,414
WHAT'S WITH THAT ANGLE?

392
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,082
- Hold that up.
- With who?

393
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:54,167
Why ask, though?

394
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,918
You wouldn't know him.

395
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:57,045
I still want to know.

396
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,255
- You wouldn't know him.
- Is it a blind date?

397
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,215
POSSIBLE DOPAMINE RUSH DETECTED

398
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,468
It's not a blind date.
I'm meeting a friend.

399
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:05,386
- Anyway, I had fun shopping.
- Me too.

400
00:14:05,428 --> 00:14:06,721
But the fun isn't over.

401
00:14:06,763 --> 00:14:08,097
We're visiting another store.

402
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:11,225
- Really?
- This place specializes

403
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,602
in curated pottery and cups.

404
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:14,062
- Amazing.
- We'll shop there.

405
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,104
I love tomatoes.

406
00:14:15,146 --> 00:14:19,192
My room is a tomato heaven
because of all the tomato-themed items.

407
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,693
Oh, my.

408
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,695
- I'm so excited.
- My gosh.

409
00:14:22,779 --> 00:14:24,489
- My gosh.
- Hello.

410
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:25,782
- Hello.
<i>- Gua sha!</i>

411
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:27,116
INSTANT AMAZEMENT

412
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,870
FROM VARIOUS TABLEWARE

413
00:14:31,329 --> 00:14:34,374
TO DELIGHTFUL HANDMADE POTTERY

414
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:39,128
CAREFULLY CURATED ITEMS

415
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,297
Isn't this ring so cute?

416
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:42,715
Try it on.

417
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,053
Help me try it.

418
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:49,222
ON TO WONHEE'S FINGER

419
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,890
So pretty.

420
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:53,017
- Want to buy a matching set?
- A friendship ring?

421
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:55,311
IN JUST 1 HOUR OF MEETING?

422
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:56,562
I'm getting those tomato earrings.

423
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:57,688
For now...

424
00:14:57,772 --> 00:14:59,774
- Tomatoes.
- Tomatoes.

425
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:00,942
I don't like them, though.

426
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:01,818
STILL IRRESISTIBLE

427
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:04,362
I like how they look.
I only eat Stevia-infused...

428
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:06,030
Gosh, check this cutie out.

429
00:15:06,114 --> 00:15:07,573
- That's so cute.
- Right?

430
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,617
- This section is stacked.
- Yeah.

431
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:11,869
I've got plenty at home,
but I want to buy more.

432
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:13,413
- The cups--
- My gosh.

433
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:15,123
- I'm all over the place.
- Check this out!

434
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,499
- Dang!
- What's this?

435
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,750
An incense holder?

436
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:19,669
So cute.

437
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,212
That's so cute.

438
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:24,340
Why do they have so many cute items?
I'm going crazy.

439
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:26,342
So cute. I'm lost here.

440
00:15:26,426 --> 00:15:27,760
I can't take this.

441
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:29,429
So cute. This is crazy.

442
00:15:29,512 --> 00:15:31,514
My gosh!

443
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:33,349
I have to get this.

444
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:35,893
CONSUMED BY ALL THE TEMPTATION

445
00:15:35,977 --> 00:15:37,937
Wait, we should look around together.

446
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,021
COMES TO HER SENSES

447
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,857
"Delicious food makes me happy."

448
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,192
- So relatable.
- Check this out. So cute.

449
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,027
I'm getting this, too.

450
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:46,737
That's so you.

451
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:48,030
That smiley face.

452
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,365
DELICIOUS FOOD MAKES ME HAPPY

453
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,284
CUTIES MAKE ME SO HAPPY

454
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:53,369
- Isn't Mangwon-dong fabulous?
- Totally.

455
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:55,872
The area is filled
with stores like this one.

456
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,498
I'm coming back alone.

457
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:58,583
I'm a loner, you see.

458
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,001
I'll come with you.

459
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,545
I'D LOVE THAT

460
00:16:02,587 --> 00:16:03,421
EXCLAIMING AGAIN

461
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,256
"Drink water regularly."

462
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:08,384
That should definitely increase
your daily water intake.

463
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:10,470
Isn't this cute, too?

464
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:13,055
Just rub it with your thumb.
It's really soothing.

465
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,557
It's just the right size.

466
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,100
RELAXED
FIDDLING

467
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,728
Shall we get one each? What do you think?

468
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:20,938
- I'm obsessed.
- Totally.

469
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,398
You like it so much.

470
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:24,400
- I want the turtle.
- Make it two.

471
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,402
I'll take this one.

472
00:16:26,486 --> 00:16:27,320
SECOND MATCHING ITEM

473
00:16:27,612 --> 00:16:29,906
- Nothing catching your eye?
- I'm actually torn.

474
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:30,823
- Get this.
- Really?

475
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:33,075
- That's the one you pick for me?
- Yeah.

476
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:34,452
- Okay.
- This one's yours.

477
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:36,454
- We'll get these here.
- I'd like to pay.

478
00:16:36,537 --> 00:16:38,372
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

479
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,751
A LARGE PILE

480
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:44,712
I didn't mean to get more cups
because I have enough at home.

481
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:45,922
Just how many did you get?

482
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,298
- Wait.
- I get it now.

483
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,925
I live alone, but I have 15 cups.

484
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,885
Do you buy all the cute cups you see?

485
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,929
That one broke my resolve.

486
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,723
I can skip cute cups,
but not a unique one like that.

487
00:16:55,765 --> 00:16:59,101
It sure is unique. It's one of a kind.

488
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:00,269
So special.

489
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:02,772
ALL NEATLY PACKAGED
Could I pay first?

490
00:17:03,314 --> 00:17:04,273
Charles.

491
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:06,442
- They're on me.
- Thank you.

492
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:08,236
Thank you, boss.

493
00:17:08,611 --> 00:17:10,821
Well, you don't have to call me that.

494
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:13,115
I didn't offer to pay
to hear that from you.

495
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:14,992
No, whoever pays is the boss.

496
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,452
Come on.

497
00:17:16,494 --> 00:17:19,288
It's great getting all the credit
on the company's dime.

498
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:23,000
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

499
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:24,460
Thank you.

500
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:27,672
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

501
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,257
WITH BAGS OF GOODIES

502
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,217
<i>- I'm having so much fun.</i>
<i>- Me too.</i>

503
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,218
ON TO THE THIRD STOP

504
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:37,473
It really feels
like I'm on <i>Guerrilla Date</i>.

505
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:39,308
CLUTCHING TIGHTLY

506
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,977
With the whole world watching us.

507
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,478
I'm down with it. I love attention.

508
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,396
- Really?
- Yeah.

509
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:45,356
- I've run before.
- Seriously?

510
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:49,569
People kept recognizing me,
so I felt self-conscious.

511
00:17:49,652 --> 00:17:54,240
Whenever I hear murmurs of my name
or my agency name,

512
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:55,658
- I just run away.
- Tell me.

513
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:57,868
You don't get out much, do you?

514
00:17:57,952 --> 00:17:59,495
No, I just stay at the dorm.

515
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:02,290
- Here it is. I was here just yesterday.
- "Chaeg Bar"?

516
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,708
<i>Amazing.</i>

517
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:04,750
CHARLES' FAVORITE PLACE

518
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:07,336
Here we are. Killer vibes, right?

519
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,797
Nice. I didn't know
there was a place like this.

520
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:11,841
- Hello.
- Welcome.

521
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:14,176
Hello. Oh, he knows you're a regular.

522
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,261
REGULAR'S PERK

523
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,846
- Hello.
- Hello.

524
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:20,016
I've visited a bar like this
and fell in love.

525
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:23,102
MELLOW VIBES

526
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:25,438
WITH BOOKS TO ENJOY

527
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:29,859
A PLACE WHERE YOU CAN READ AND DRINK
TO FIND OUT WHAT YOU LIKE

528
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,653
- Do you enjoy reading?
- Well...

529
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:35,323
- It feels kind of weird to--
- But you enjoy it.

530
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,490
Just say it out loud.

531
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:39,410
- With confidence.
- I do read. I like it a little bit.

532
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,203
But I get why you're so resistant.

533
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:44,915
Saying you like reading
can make you sound like a know-it-all.

534
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:47,376
- Exactly.
- Pretentious, even.

535
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,712
- That's why I couldn't say it.
- I get it.

536
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:51,547
I regret saying that sometimes.

537
00:18:51,589 --> 00:18:53,841
When I hit the explore page
on social media,

538
00:18:53,883 --> 00:18:55,301
I see posts about the books I recommended.

539
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:59,180
But the seven books I recommended
were the only ones I read that year.

540
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,348
NO MORE BOOKS TO RECOMMEND

541
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:02,475
- Want to take a look?
- I'd love that.

542
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:05,561
Do you like fiction?

543
00:19:05,645 --> 00:19:08,189
I read essays the most and then fiction.

544
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,816
I rarely read essays.
My favorite genre is fiction.

545
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:13,277
I highly recommend this one.

546
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:15,488
<i>- Aimez-vous Brahms?</i>
- This one?

547
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:17,865
It's a classic romance novel.

548
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:21,410
In summary,
the protagonist is feeling torn

549
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:24,372
between her long-term boyfriend
and a younger man.

550
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:25,456
Interesting, right?

551
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,083
- It sure is.
- Try this.

552
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,250
- It's good.
- Okay.

553
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:29,251
I'll try this one.

554
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:30,419
Can I make a recommendation?

555
00:19:30,503 --> 00:19:32,213
- Sure.
- It's been adapted into a TV show.

556
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,423
<i>- Hunter With a Scalpel.</i>
- What's the genre?

557
00:19:34,465 --> 00:19:35,383
It's a thriller.

558
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:37,927
- And they made a TV show?
- That's what I heard.

559
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:39,136
It's incredible.

560
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:40,763
I finished it in one sitting.

561
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:43,349
- Let me write it down.
<i>- Hunter With a Scalpel.</i>

562
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,768
Okay, I'll make sure to read it.

563
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,937
Shall we order some drinks?

564
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,940
They have a fun selection of drinks.

565
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:53,109
<i>Check this out.</i>

566
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:55,194
<i>All the cocktails are named after books.</i>

567
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,737
INSPIRED BY BOOKS AND AUTHORS

568
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:58,114
What should we order?

569
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,198
Let's get a recommendation.

570
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:02,618
Could you recommend
something fruity and fresh?

571
00:20:02,702 --> 00:20:04,787
Why don't you try "Call Me By Your Name"?

572
00:20:04,829 --> 00:20:05,913
Oh, right.

573
00:20:05,955 --> 00:20:07,957
<i>- It's good. I'll get it.</i>
<i>- So it's sweet and fruity.</i>

574
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,834
<i>- The sky-blue drink?</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

575
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:10,751
<i>I'm getting that.</i>

576
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:11,794
I'll get that, too.

577
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,045
FOLLOWING THE OWNER'S SUGGESTION

578
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:14,547
- The same ones?
- Yes, please.

579
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,466
You know this place inside and out.

580
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,802
- You must've been here often.
- Here's the funny thing.

581
00:20:19,844 --> 00:20:23,973
I came here yesterday
to have this drink about April.

582
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:26,058
- The one that had April in its name?
- Right.

583
00:20:26,142 --> 00:20:27,977
The one inspired by a Haruki novella.

584
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,311
I have a thing, you see.

585
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:32,481
In summer, I read a book
that has "summer" in the title.

586
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,525
- In August--
- You like the themed stuff.

587
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:35,484
Exactly.

588
00:20:35,526 --> 00:20:39,530
I had to come here in April,
so I even took a cab to get here in time.

589
00:20:39,822 --> 00:20:44,160
But he suddenly asked why I came
when I was coming again the next day.

590
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,412
I was so startled.

591
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:48,998
I only check the script
on the day of the shoot.

592
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:52,585
I didn't know
I would be coming here today.

593
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:55,337
I had no idea we'd be here together.

594
00:20:55,421 --> 00:20:57,798
- So all that was for nothing.
- Yeah, so as it turns out,

595
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:00,259
- I'm visiting here two days in a row.
- That's nice.

596
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:02,136
- What did you read yesterday?
- About that.

597
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:04,597
- All the drinks are book-inspired, right?
- Did you read this?

598
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,892
- I read this over the cocktail.
- A cocktail and a book about April?

599
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:10,352
That's a perfect combo for April.

600
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,897
- That's my recommendation for you.
- That's fun.

601
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,857
- People eat seasonal food.
- Right.

602
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:18,194
Just like that,
we can build a seasonal routine.

603
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:23,449
That gives you something
to look forward to every season.

604
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:26,410
- You want to figure out your taste.
- I love that.

605
00:21:26,494 --> 00:21:28,704
When you have established
a seasonal routine,

606
00:21:28,788 --> 00:21:30,539
you'll grow to love the seasons more.

607
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:32,041
That's a good idea.

608
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:34,543
Can I ask what your life was like at 20?

609
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:35,461
My life at 20?

610
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:36,879
How should I put this?

611
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:38,130
It was a dark time.

612
00:21:38,339 --> 00:21:40,049
WITH UNCLEAR FUTURE

613
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:41,217
Totally dark?

614
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:42,843
I was lost back then.

615
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:47,181
So I don't really have
good memories of that time.

616
00:21:47,223 --> 00:21:50,226
But I believe that time has led me
to where I am now.

617
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:51,143
VALUABLE EXPERIENCE

618
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:52,144
That's nice.

619
00:21:52,228 --> 00:21:55,940
What was the first thing
that helped you through it?

620
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,233
Fangirling.

621
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:58,442
On who?

622
00:21:58,526 --> 00:22:00,236
I was a huge fan of iKON.

623
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,946
Bobby was my bias.

624
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:03,447
Why am I talking like an idol?

625
00:22:03,531 --> 00:22:06,242
- I didn't know you were in this industry.
- Anyway...

626
00:22:06,283 --> 00:22:08,494
- I was a huge fan of him.
- I know him.

627
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:11,330
People associate age 20
with new experiences, right?

628
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:14,041
For me, fangirling was like my first love.

629
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:18,087
My life was chaos,
but iKON gave me something to hold on to.

630
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:20,047
They're like your first love.

631
00:22:20,089 --> 00:22:20,965
- Totally.
- Wait,

632
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:23,717
it sounds like your heart was full.
Why were you lost?

633
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,262
I didn't get into any of the colleges
I applied to.

634
00:22:26,554 --> 00:22:29,348
I ended up going to the one
I didn't want to.

635
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:32,059
I didn't think I could bear
the stress of CSAT again.

636
00:22:32,101 --> 00:22:37,606
I became really bitter because of college.

637
00:22:38,607 --> 00:22:39,984
- I just--
- Negativity took over?

638
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,111
Yes, it overwhelmed me.

639
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:45,239
<i>- How sad.</i>
<i>- That phase lasted until I was 23.</i>

640
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:47,700
<i>- It can be hard to turn it around.</i>
<i>- Actually,</i>

641
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:50,744
I regained my cheerful self
after starting a YouTube channel.

642
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:52,037
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

643
00:22:52,121 --> 00:22:54,290
- Here are your drinks.
- Thank you.

644
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:55,165
COCKTAILS ARE HERE

645
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:58,335
REFRESHING COCKTAILS

646
00:22:58,419 --> 00:23:02,298
IN THE SHADE OF THE CLEAR AZURE SKY

647
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:04,550
CELEBRATING THEIR FIRST MEETING

648
00:23:08,429 --> 00:23:09,638
What about your assignment?

649
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:11,348
Oh, right.

650
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:14,059
<i>- We totally forgot about it.</i>
<i>- I know.</i>

651
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:16,770
"Twenty questions for Wonhee"
for my self-discovery.

652
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,939
"What changed for you after turning 20?"

653
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:20,774
To be honest...

654
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:23,027
I mean, I didn't go to college.

655
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:27,656
Because I'm an idol,
it's just no end of work.

656
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:29,575
The only thing that has changed

657
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:32,536
- Just drinks?
- is that I can now drink alcohol.

658
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,122
- Everything else is the same.
- Right, but hear me out.

659
00:23:35,164 --> 00:23:38,250
When you keep thinking
that your life has to change at 20,

660
00:23:38,334 --> 00:23:40,044
you'll only end up disappointed.

661
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:40,961
I mean it.

662
00:23:41,003 --> 00:23:45,090
Expectations tied to age
are just another social construct.

663
00:23:45,174 --> 00:23:46,258
- I know.
- Right?

664
00:23:46,675 --> 00:23:48,928
"What comment do you get most often
after turning 20?"

665
00:23:49,011 --> 00:23:50,471
"How's being 20?"

666
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:52,389
- People ask that a lot?
- Yeah.

667
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:55,434
What was the most memorable comment
you heard as a 20-year-old?

668
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,019
"Make a lot of memories."

669
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:58,479
"Go on trips."

670
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,940
Especially the one about trips.
But that just made me think,

671
00:24:01,023 --> 00:24:03,484
"Are you paying for my trips?"

672
00:24:03,525 --> 00:24:06,153
"I don't have any money.
How am I supposed to travel?"

673
00:24:06,195 --> 00:24:08,113
Have you been on trips?

674
00:24:08,197 --> 00:24:10,074
Not after I turned 20.

675
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:11,492
None.

676
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:14,036
Back when I was in school,
my family traveled together.

677
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:16,246
We visited Taiwan and Japan
once in a while.

678
00:24:16,330 --> 00:24:18,290
Don't you want to travel?

679
00:24:18,374 --> 00:24:20,459
- I'd love to.
- I see.

680
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:22,711
- Have you travelled?
- Yeah, multiple times.

681
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:23,879
Were they therapeutic?

682
00:24:23,921 --> 00:24:26,006
Not exactly, but they leave you
with great memories.

683
00:24:26,048 --> 00:24:29,259
When you look back,
regular days are a blur.

684
00:24:29,343 --> 00:24:31,387
But trips leave you lasting memories,

685
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:34,848
<i>so you and your friends</i>
<i>can reminisce about it together.</i>

686
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,350
<i>I highly recommend traveling.</i>

687
00:24:36,392 --> 00:24:39,895
<i>Now that you're an adult,</i>
<i>you have more freedom.</i>

688
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:41,480
- Of course, you're busy,
- Right.

689
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:44,233
but when you have the time,
travel with your childhood friends.

690
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:45,192
GO ON AN ADVENTURE

691
00:24:45,234 --> 00:24:46,318
Somewhere close, like Japan.

692
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:48,070
"What's an ideal adult in your mind?"

693
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:50,072
It doesn't feel
like you've become an adult.

694
00:24:50,114 --> 00:24:51,198
- No.
- Thought so.

695
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,199
Just legal.

696
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:53,742
When do you think you'll be a real adult?

697
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:54,660
At 30.

698
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:57,037
- Same, so I'm not an adult yet.
- At age 30.

699
00:24:57,079 --> 00:24:58,998
What kind of adult do you want to be?

700
00:24:59,081 --> 00:25:00,124
Well...

701
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:03,752
I'd like to be someone
who looks good in a black suit

702
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:05,671
and high heels.

703
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:08,757
I thought I'd wear heels when I grew up.

704
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:11,010
Because on TV,
the women are always clicking around

705
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:12,594
- in heels.
- My thoughts exactly.

706
00:25:12,678 --> 00:25:14,096
But when I wear them,

707
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:16,682
I walk like a water deer in heels.

708
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:19,101
Back when I was terrible with heels,

709
00:25:19,143 --> 00:25:21,937
I couldn't walk from the pain,
so my friends supported me.

710
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:25,649
- Oh, no. Are you flat-footed?
- In the end, I bought cheap slippers.

711
00:25:26,025 --> 00:25:27,234
- I'm not sure.
- I am, actually.

712
00:25:27,276 --> 00:25:29,945
Heels hurt my feet, so I rarely wear them.

713
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:32,614
"What are the three words
that best describe you?"

714
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:34,867
I'm not sure who I am as a person.

715
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:36,535
You've spent a day with me.

716
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:38,120
Can you pick them for me?

717
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:40,330
First, you're chill.

718
00:25:40,414 --> 00:25:42,541
- Thanks, I'll write it down.
- And then,

719
00:25:42,624 --> 00:25:44,710
you're highly self-aware.

720
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,128
Highly...

721
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,005
IS SHE A SHRINK?
Highly self-aware.

722
00:25:48,088 --> 00:25:49,965
You're very sensitive
to others' mood changes.

723
00:25:50,049 --> 00:25:54,053
You're the quickest
to notice that about me.

724
00:25:54,136 --> 00:25:56,638
- Really?
- You're the first to catch it so fast.

725
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,807
- How did I seem to you?
- You?

726
00:25:58,849 --> 00:26:00,768
You're so chill.

727
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:01,852
Let me think.

728
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:04,772
I was surprised to find... Shoot.

729
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:07,066
It's such a shame I'm not so articulate.

730
00:26:07,149 --> 00:26:09,109
Did my composure surprise you?

731
00:26:09,151 --> 00:26:09,985
No.

732
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:11,195
You're more...

733
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:12,154
THAT WAS QUICK

734
00:26:12,196 --> 00:26:13,155
LEADING QUESTION FAILED

735
00:26:13,197 --> 00:26:15,324
- That's not you.
- Aren't I composed today?

736
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:17,076
- No, not quite.
- No?

737
00:26:17,159 --> 00:26:18,494
I guess I thought wrong.

738
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:20,996
- You're very sharp.
- Really?

739
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,456
And you're polite.

740
00:26:24,166 --> 00:26:25,417
Thanks for the compliments.

741
00:26:25,501 --> 00:26:26,335
SATISFIED

742
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:28,921
"What is your least favorite trait?"
I've got a long list.

743
00:26:29,004 --> 00:26:31,340
Me too.
I don't like that I'm an overthinker.

744
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:32,674
- Seriously?
- What about you?

745
00:26:32,758 --> 00:26:34,259
I'm far too impatient.

746
00:26:34,343 --> 00:26:36,470
I talk, walk, and eat fast.

747
00:26:37,596 --> 00:26:40,474
I'm so impatient
that slow people frustrate me.

748
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:42,184
But I get it.
I feel that way sometimes, too.

749
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:46,355
So I admire people
who move leisurely at their own pace.

750
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:48,690
I find that very attractive.

751
00:26:48,982 --> 00:26:52,027
- I used to prefer quiet men.
- I see.

752
00:26:53,654 --> 00:26:55,364
COSPLAYING A RELAXED ADULT

753
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,032
Can I ask about your ideal type?

754
00:26:57,074 --> 00:26:58,158
My ideal type?

755
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,701
That's an excellent question.

756
00:26:59,993 --> 00:27:01,703
SUDDENLY MORE ENTHUSIASTIC

757
00:27:01,787 --> 00:27:03,539
- Because--
- I asked so many questions to her,

758
00:27:03,622 --> 00:27:05,124
but I got my first approval now.

759
00:27:05,207 --> 00:27:06,208
SUDDENLY FEELING EMPTY

760
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:08,418
It's because I've changed my mind
about my ideal type.

761
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:11,755
Actually, I've openly shared this
so many times.

762
00:27:11,839 --> 00:27:12,881
Who was your ideal type?

763
00:27:12,923 --> 00:27:14,216
It wasn't an individual.

764
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:17,845
I hoped to meet
a quiet and gentle introvert.

765
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,555
But not these days.

766
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,098
I'd like to meet someone like me.

767
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:23,308
- Someone outgoing like you?
- Yeah.

768
00:27:23,392 --> 00:27:25,185
I recently had an epiphany.

769
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:28,188
I'm still attracted to my opposites.
They make my heart race.

770
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,732
- But we just don't click.
- I get it.

771
00:27:31,233 --> 00:27:33,068
I've come to think

772
00:27:33,110 --> 00:27:35,737
that I'd hit it off better
with someone who's like me

773
00:27:35,821 --> 00:27:37,656
than someone who checks every box.

774
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:39,283
So I've updated my ideal type.

775
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:40,284
FROM INTROVERT TO EXTROVERT

776
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:43,412
How would you act
if your dream guy were in front of you?

777
00:27:43,704 --> 00:27:45,414
That's a real challenge for me.

778
00:27:45,497 --> 00:27:46,707
I actually cried a few days ago.

779
00:27:46,748 --> 00:27:48,000
- Why?
- I mean,

780
00:27:48,083 --> 00:27:51,503
all my friends said I acted
like I'd never dated before.

781
00:27:51,587 --> 00:27:53,297
- I also get that a lot.
- The thing is,

782
00:27:53,380 --> 00:27:55,883
I found it so shocking

783
00:27:55,924 --> 00:27:59,803
because I thought
I was so savvy and cunning.

784
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:01,013
YOU DID, HUH?

785
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:04,099
I always thought I was such a player.

786
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,184
- Really?
- Yeah.

787
00:28:05,267 --> 00:28:07,144
I don't think of myself like that.

788
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:08,854
I've never seen someone
who has never dated think that way.

789
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:09,855
Are you serious?

790
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:12,191
All my friends asked the same question.

791
00:28:12,274 --> 00:28:13,817
So basically...

792
00:28:13,901 --> 00:28:17,571
Their comments about
how clumsy I am in relationships

793
00:28:17,613 --> 00:28:19,198
made me tear up in the end.

794
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,658
I don't want to be so awkward.

795
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:23,243
I want to be a pro.

796
00:28:23,285 --> 00:28:24,828
YOU CAN'T LAUGH

797
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:27,164
I didn't know I was chill
until people told me so.

798
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:28,957
SPEECHLESS

799
00:28:28,999 --> 00:28:30,292
ZERO SELF-AWARENESS

800
00:28:30,334 --> 00:28:32,002
But you laugh out loud like this.

801
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:35,422
You don't realize how you look like
when you laugh.

802
00:28:35,464 --> 00:28:37,382
I assumed everyone laughed like me.

803
00:28:37,466 --> 00:28:41,303
Earlier, the production crew told me
I was prettier in person.

804
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,263
- That's so true.
- So I smiled,

805
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:45,974
but they told me not to smile like that.

806
00:28:46,016 --> 00:28:47,142
Here's the replay.

807
00:28:47,184 --> 00:28:48,977
This is how I smiled.

808
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:51,480
That was me feeling shy.

809
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:53,899
That was what I wanted to convey.

810
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:55,067
I ROLL MY EYES WHEN I FEEL SHY

811
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,236
Your laughs are fine,
but the eye-rolling smile isn't.

812
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:59,571
Anyway, my point is...

813
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:01,365
It's hard to know
how other people see you.

814
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:02,491
CHARLES' SELF-DISCOVERY

815
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:04,368
You've had a series about dating.

816
00:29:04,451 --> 00:29:05,911
Who did you like best?

817
00:29:06,286 --> 00:29:07,329
SO DIRECT

818
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:09,957
- Who did you click with the most?
- The most?

819
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:11,667
No one, actually.

820
00:29:11,959 --> 00:29:13,210
THAT WAS TOO HONEST

821
00:29:13,293 --> 00:29:15,045
Was I too blunt? Let me rephrase.

822
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:18,090
Everyone was great,
but I didn't feel a spark with anyone.

823
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:20,008
What's your ideal type?

824
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:22,052
I don't have a concrete type.

825
00:29:22,678 --> 00:29:23,845
Just...

826
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:28,433
But trust me, your ideal type evolves
just like your taste does.

827
00:29:28,517 --> 00:29:30,435
Take my case, for example.

828
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:32,688
My ideal type did a 180
now that I'm a few years older.

829
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:35,941
Everyone would find
these qualities attractive,

830
00:29:36,024 --> 00:29:37,818
so I'm not sure if it means much.

831
00:29:37,859 --> 00:29:40,195
Basically, I want someone
with a good personality.

832
00:29:40,237 --> 00:29:41,989
A kind person.

833
00:29:42,030 --> 00:29:43,615
But I also want him to be funny.

834
00:29:43,699 --> 00:29:46,159
My ideal guy has to be funny and tactful.

835
00:29:46,201 --> 00:29:47,286
That's about it.

836
00:29:47,369 --> 00:29:51,123
Has anyone acted
so outrageously flirty toward you?

837
00:29:51,206 --> 00:29:53,625
To be honest,
I have very strict standards.

838
00:29:53,709 --> 00:29:55,544
Whoever texts me is a flirt.

839
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:58,630
JUDGE CHARLES IS A TOUGH ONE

840
00:29:58,714 --> 00:30:01,008
I meant what I said.

841
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:05,053
"Don't text me if you're not interested."
That's what I want...

842
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:07,973
That's what I want as my status message.

843
00:30:08,432 --> 00:30:10,767
"Don't text me if you're not interested."

844
00:30:10,851 --> 00:30:12,644
- Let me explain.
- Thank goodness I'm a girl.

845
00:30:12,728 --> 00:30:17,232
A text would make me think,
"Do we have something going on?"

846
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:21,570
I wouldn't go full delulu,
but I'd wonder if he has feelings for me.

847
00:30:21,737 --> 00:30:23,780
- That's not irrational, right?
- Right.

848
00:30:23,864 --> 00:30:25,615
So even a text counts as flirting.

849
00:30:25,699 --> 00:30:27,576
- So strict.
- But only in cases

850
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:30,787
where it hasn't been set in stone
that we're only friends.

851
00:30:30,871 --> 00:30:32,289
What if it's for work?

852
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:34,166
- That's totally okay.
- Right?

853
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:35,500
How do you define love?

854
00:30:35,584 --> 00:30:37,419
OUT OF THE BLUE?

855
00:30:37,502 --> 00:30:39,713
PHENOMENAL HOSTING SKILLS

856
00:30:39,755 --> 00:30:43,592
I sometimes host a talk show
on my YouTube channel,

857
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:45,135
and that's one of my signature questions.

858
00:30:45,594 --> 00:30:46,595
Definition of love?

859
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:47,763
That's so difficult.

860
00:30:48,263 --> 00:30:49,181
To me, it's comfort.

861
00:30:49,264 --> 00:30:52,184
I just don't like friction these days.

862
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,478
- But that's too broad.
- Maybe.

863
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:56,480
- That'd cover friends, too.
- I love them.

864
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:58,231
Yes, but my point is...

865
00:30:58,273 --> 00:31:00,525
- Rather than just romantic love,
- The romantic love...

866
00:31:00,609 --> 00:31:02,361
- I'm covering all kinds of love.
- On the whole?

867
00:31:03,153 --> 00:31:03,987
On the whole...

868
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:06,865
- I'd go with familiarity.
- Familiarity?

869
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:10,660
- Why?
- I love it.

870
00:31:10,744 --> 00:31:12,287
It's such a good answer.

871
00:31:12,371 --> 00:31:15,165
There's a song about this.

872
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:17,876
One More Chance released this song,
"I Think of You."

873
00:31:17,959 --> 00:31:19,086
The song goes,

874
00:31:19,127 --> 00:31:22,381
"You chase the thrill of something new.
But I find love in familiarity."

875
00:31:23,131 --> 00:31:24,674
- You didn't know that, did you?
- No.

876
00:31:24,758 --> 00:31:26,468
You should try writing your own lyrics.

877
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:28,220
"Love is familiarity"? You go, girl.

878
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:30,305
But it's so easy to forget the close ones.

879
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:31,431
That's the issue.

880
00:31:31,473 --> 00:31:33,308
- So deep.
- About love...

881
00:31:33,475 --> 00:31:35,394
That comment was gold.

882
00:31:35,477 --> 00:31:37,979
- I'm so inspired.
- Really?

883
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:40,399
I was worried that sounded cringey.

884
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:43,026
- Really?
- Yeah.

885
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:45,904
- Did your amazing answer weird you out?
- No, it's just that

886
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:49,741
your reaction caught me off guard.

887
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:51,493
I should've reined it in.

888
00:31:51,535 --> 00:31:52,828
20-YEAR-OLDS ARE A MYSTERY

889
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,621
Do you ever act cute around people?

890
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:56,248
Just around people I'm really close with.

891
00:31:56,331 --> 00:31:59,793
The only people I act cute around
are my parents.

892
00:31:59,835 --> 00:32:01,753
I act shamelessly cute around them.

893
00:32:01,837 --> 00:32:03,505
I don't want anyone to see me like that.

894
00:32:03,547 --> 00:32:05,048
Do you go, "Mommy"?

895
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:06,341
I talk like a baby.

896
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:08,176
- Wow, really?
- I do that.

897
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:10,470
How would it feel
to have a daughter like you?

898
00:32:10,512 --> 00:32:12,472
Probably a handful.

899
00:32:12,514 --> 00:32:14,015
NO WAY!

900
00:32:14,057 --> 00:32:15,600
Do you act cute around people?

901
00:32:15,684 --> 00:32:17,144
I'm just like you.

902
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,270
It depends on people.

903
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:19,771
How are you around your parents?

904
00:32:19,855 --> 00:32:22,023
I'm like a strict eldest son.

905
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:23,024
- A strict eldest?
- "Mother!"

906
00:32:23,108 --> 00:32:24,401
SO DISCIPLINED

907
00:32:24,651 --> 00:32:25,986
"Father!"

908
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:27,946
I'm like a drill sergeant.

909
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:30,323
I speak really softly to my parents.

910
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:32,909
I act even cuter
when the other person dislikes it.

911
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:36,371
If they push me away, I act even cuter.

912
00:32:36,413 --> 00:32:37,706
- That makes it fun.
- Exactly.

913
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,709
Seung-heon hates it,
so I act the cutest around him.

914
00:32:40,792 --> 00:32:42,419
I totally get it.

915
00:32:42,502 --> 00:32:44,504
- You overdo it around people like that.
- Yeah.

916
00:32:44,546 --> 00:32:45,881
I even talk with a lisp.

917
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:47,757
POOR SEUNG-HEON

918
00:32:47,841 --> 00:32:49,259
I lay it on as thick as I can.

919
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:51,553
I'll tell you the funniest thing
he's ever said to me.

920
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:53,138
In the end, he went,

921
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:56,224
"Save this energy
for someone you actually like!"

922
00:32:56,308 --> 00:32:58,059
When I'm around my crush,

923
00:32:58,143 --> 00:32:59,478
- I usually act cool.
- How?

924
00:32:59,853 --> 00:33:01,605
Do you use your drill sergeant voice?

925
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,565
I'm like, "What do you mean?"

926
00:33:03,607 --> 00:33:06,693
I act cold around my crush,
but I act cute around others.

927
00:33:06,735 --> 00:33:08,487
Seung-heon begged me
to do that to my crush.

928
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,490
That's understandable
from his point of view.

929
00:33:11,573 --> 00:33:14,493
What makes you feel loved?

930
00:33:14,576 --> 00:33:16,495
An enthusiastic response.

931
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:17,913
- Really?
- For instance,

932
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:20,582
my fans get excited
over the smallest things.

933
00:33:20,624 --> 00:33:22,876
They would go, "My gosh."

934
00:33:23,335 --> 00:33:26,463
When I want my parents
to be worried for me,

935
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:29,883
- I'd pretend I was getting sick.
- I see.

936
00:33:29,925 --> 00:33:32,093
Their concern makes me feel loved.

937
00:33:32,761 --> 00:33:34,763
- What about you?
- For me,

938
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:37,098
it's when they take an interest
in my daily life.

939
00:33:37,182 --> 00:33:40,185
I love it. One of my friends
once texted me, "What's up?"

940
00:33:40,268 --> 00:33:41,645
I replied, "Oh, I'm so touched."

941
00:33:41,937 --> 00:33:43,813
STARVED FOR ATTENTION

942
00:33:43,897 --> 00:33:45,607
She was like, "About what?"

943
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:47,943
The question itself was so touching.

944
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,653
Nobody asks that anymore.

945
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:51,321
"What's up?" "Thank you."

946
00:33:51,821 --> 00:33:54,449
Trust me. That's the way to my heart.

947
00:33:54,533 --> 00:33:55,784
Just ask me what's up.

948
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:56,952
AND THAT'S ENOUGH

949
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:59,162
"If you could get away right now,
where would you go?"

950
00:33:59,246 --> 00:34:00,622
There's only one destination for me.

951
00:34:00,664 --> 00:34:01,831
- Can I guess?
- Hawaii.

952
00:34:01,915 --> 00:34:03,375
I wanted to guess.

953
00:34:04,251 --> 00:34:05,919
Sorry, I got ahead of myself.

954
00:34:06,336 --> 00:34:08,505
The crazy thing is, mine's Hawaii, too.

955
00:34:08,588 --> 00:34:10,632
- I mean it. No cap.
- Seriously?

956
00:34:10,674 --> 00:34:11,508
- For real?
- Sure.

957
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:12,842
Hawaii is at the top of my list,

958
00:34:12,926 --> 00:34:14,636
- followed by Australia.
- Australia?

959
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:16,429
My second choice is Okinawa.

960
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:18,265
Okinawa is so you.

961
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:20,058
- I mean...
- Are you just going along,

962
00:34:20,141 --> 00:34:21,643
- or are you--
- It suits you.

963
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:23,019
You're basically Okinawa in human form.

964
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:24,187
WHAT?

965
00:34:24,271 --> 00:34:25,939
Your clear and fresh image

966
00:34:25,981 --> 00:34:27,857
is a perfect match
for Okinawa's emerald ocean.

967
00:34:27,941 --> 00:34:30,235
I've been compared to the ocean,
but not to a city.

968
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:31,861
WONHEE, OKINAWA PERSONIFIED

969
00:34:31,945 --> 00:34:34,531
There's a place
I'd like to recommend to you.

970
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:35,490
Where is it?

971
00:34:35,532 --> 00:34:38,660
It doesn't fit your image per se,
but please visit California.

972
00:34:38,702 --> 00:34:39,661
- Have you been there?
- Yes.

973
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:41,329
- How was it?
- Just two weeks ago.

974
00:34:41,371 --> 00:34:42,497
<i>- Tell me more.</i>
<i>- I loved it.</i>

975
00:34:42,539 --> 00:34:44,749
<i>I had a fabulous time.</i>
<i>I highly recommend it.</i>

976
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:46,668
<i>I'll consider it.</i>

977
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:51,172
I want to see you serving
hot-girl looks over there.

978
00:34:51,256 --> 00:34:52,924
So this is about your curiosity?

979
00:34:53,008 --> 00:34:55,427
You wanted me to go California
to satisfy your curiosity?

980
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,220
- Yes, out of simple curiosity.
- Really?

981
00:34:57,304 --> 00:34:58,597
- Basically,
- It's purely personal.

982
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:01,433
you just wanted to see me
dressed up like a hot girl?

983
00:35:01,516 --> 00:35:03,643
So that's why you suggested California
out of the blue.

984
00:35:03,685 --> 00:35:05,854
- I want to see your pics.
- I got it.

985
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:08,982
I hear your goal is to meet
the one within the year.

986
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:12,235
Oh, right. I wondered how you knew.

987
00:35:12,319 --> 00:35:13,778
I was shocked for a second.

988
00:35:13,862 --> 00:35:15,905
- That's true.
- Have you met him?

989
00:35:15,989 --> 00:35:18,533
I've met many guys,
but I don't know if I've met the one yet.

990
00:35:18,575 --> 00:35:19,701
I've been praying.

991
00:35:19,743 --> 00:35:20,619
RESORTING TO PRAYERS

992
00:35:20,702 --> 00:35:23,955
Does someone particular come to mind?

993
00:35:24,039 --> 00:35:25,123
LET ME JOG YOUR MEMORY

994
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:27,083
I can't say his name on camera.

995
00:35:28,043 --> 00:35:29,628
So you have someone!

996
00:35:29,711 --> 00:35:31,046
- I do, so--
- Who is it?

997
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:32,213
You won't know, anyway.

998
00:35:32,255 --> 00:35:33,256
STILL CRAVES THE HOT GOSSIP

999
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:34,174
You want his name?

1000
00:35:34,215 --> 00:35:35,884
Tell me more about him.

1001
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:37,594
Want to know my goal?

1002
00:35:37,677 --> 00:35:39,095
- Does this go online in July?
- Yes.

1003
00:35:39,179 --> 00:35:42,223
I'd like to be in a relationship by then.

1004
00:35:42,307 --> 00:35:43,516
I think you will.

1005
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,268
- Fingers crossed.
- I'll be rooting for you.

1006
00:35:45,352 --> 00:35:46,728
- Wish me luck.
- Of course.

1007
00:35:46,770 --> 00:35:49,564
- "What do you want to hear the most?"
- Me?

1008
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:51,524
What about you?

1009
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,735
- Me? "What's up?"
- "What's up?"

1010
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:55,403
"What's up?" "I'm on a shoot with Wonhee."

1011
00:35:55,445 --> 00:35:57,572
"Right, you're on a shoot with me.
What else is up?"

1012
00:35:57,906 --> 00:35:59,783
It's about my profession.

1013
00:35:59,866 --> 00:36:01,242
As a YouTuber,

1014
00:36:01,326 --> 00:36:04,037
I open up a huge chunk of my life
to my subscribers.

1015
00:36:04,079 --> 00:36:06,706
- So no one asks me for an update.
- It's understandable.

1016
00:36:06,748 --> 00:36:08,166
But I want a proper chat.

1017
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:11,419
That's why I feel so happy
when my friends ask me for an update.

1018
00:36:11,503 --> 00:36:12,796
- That's my love language.
- I see.

1019
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,130
"What's up? I miss you."

1020
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:16,007
From Mr. Mystery, too?

1021
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:19,344
AN UNEXPECTED ATTACK

1022
00:36:19,427 --> 00:36:20,261
We're meeting tomorrow.

1023
00:36:22,097 --> 00:36:23,890
Here in Mangwon-dong.

1024
00:36:23,932 --> 00:36:26,101
Actually, I meant to come here.

1025
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:28,436
- For three days in a row?
- I almost did that.

1026
00:36:28,478 --> 00:36:29,688
But the bar closes tomorrow.

1027
00:36:30,063 --> 00:36:31,147
It's an off day for the owner.

1028
00:36:31,231 --> 00:36:32,607
WILL CHARLES START DATING SOON?

1029
00:36:32,816 --> 00:36:33,983
Something you'd like to hear?

1030
00:36:34,067 --> 00:36:35,819
For me, "Good luck."

1031
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:36,986
- Really?
- Yeah.

1032
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:38,613
When do you feel down?

1033
00:36:38,697 --> 00:36:41,574
I can't think of that,
but I know what energizes me.

1034
00:36:41,616 --> 00:36:42,742
I can guess when.

1035
00:36:42,784 --> 00:36:44,744
- When you meet fans, right?
- Yes.

1036
00:36:44,786 --> 00:36:45,995
- Wait.
- They lift my spirits.

1037
00:36:46,079 --> 00:36:46,913
I have a question.

1038
00:36:46,955 --> 00:36:49,416
I've never been on stage.

1039
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:52,502
When you see the audience cheer for you,
does that pump you up?

1040
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:53,753
- Sure.
- Really?

1041
00:36:53,795 --> 00:36:54,963
- You get pumped.
- Next question.

1042
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:58,174
When you go off-stage,
do you really get an aftershock?

1043
00:36:58,258 --> 00:36:59,759
When I come off stage, I feel more like,

1044
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:01,845
- "I did it."
- "I did it."

1045
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:03,054
Really?

1046
00:37:03,138 --> 00:37:06,266
What are you looking forward to this year?

1047
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:09,060
My group goes on a tour
for the first time.

1048
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:10,729
- Across Asia.
- Really?

1049
00:37:10,812 --> 00:37:12,897
- I'd love to go to your concert.
- I'm so excited.

1050
00:37:12,981 --> 00:37:15,024
SHY
Really? Please come.

1051
00:37:15,984 --> 00:37:18,820
It's our first tour,
so I'm really excited about it.

1052
00:37:18,987 --> 00:37:20,572
- You've got this!
- I'll do my best!

1053
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:21,656
GOOD LUCK, WONHEE

1054
00:37:21,740 --> 00:37:24,409
That's a wrap on our 20 questions.

1055
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:26,202
Did it help your self-discovery?

1056
00:37:26,286 --> 00:37:28,830
Having a talented guide like you with me

1057
00:37:28,872 --> 00:37:30,957
and visiting shops across Mangwon-dong

1058
00:37:30,999 --> 00:37:32,500
definitely helped.

1059
00:37:32,542 --> 00:37:33,793
To be perfectly honest,

1060
00:37:33,835 --> 00:37:36,504
you know how too many compliments

1061
00:37:36,588 --> 00:37:39,632
can make the other person feel
awkward and uncomfortable.

1062
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:41,092
So I really restrained myself.

1063
00:37:41,176 --> 00:37:42,010
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

1064
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:45,263
I still received so much good energy
from all your compliments.

1065
00:37:45,346 --> 00:37:47,015
- Thank you.
- I held myself back.

1066
00:37:47,056 --> 00:37:50,393
Just seeing you lifted my spirits.

1067
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:52,395
You know what? Right back at you.

1068
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:53,855
I mean that.

1069
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:55,315
But don't laugh like that.

1070
00:37:55,356 --> 00:37:56,983
Why not?

1071
00:37:57,025 --> 00:37:58,359
- Wasn't I cute?
- That was cute.

1072
00:37:58,401 --> 00:37:59,778
- "Why not?"
- Got it.

1073
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:00,695
Should I do it again?

1074
00:38:00,779 --> 00:38:03,114
If someone stops me from laughing,
I'll go, "Why not?"

1075
00:38:03,198 --> 00:38:04,908
You're not supposed to close your eyes.

1076
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:06,117
Like this, then?

1077
00:38:06,534 --> 00:38:07,952
- Don't roll your eyes.
- Okay.

1078
00:38:08,036 --> 00:38:09,037
Got it.

1079
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:10,205
BUMPY ROAD TO ACTING CUTE

1080
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:14,709
